            <ArticleTitle>Acute myocardial infarction with normal coronary arteries. In vivo demonstration of coronary thrombosis during the acute episode.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>553-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases with acute myocardial infarction are presented. Both had thrombotic occlusion of the infarct-related artery. Following successful thrombolysis with streptokinase, coronary angiography was normal. These cases prove that &quot;myocardial infarction with normal coronaries&quot; can be associated with coronary thrombosis in the acute stage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
